  Summary

  The project plan breaks down the refactoring into 5 phases over 10-13 weeks:

  1. Foundation & Registry Module (3 weeks) - Create new activation binary and Registry Module
  2. Executive & Process Management (3 weeks) - Enhanced watchdog with better lifecycle management
  3. Bash Script Consolidation (2 weeks) - Simplify activation scripts with replayEnv()
  4. Testing & Integration (3 weeks) - Comprehensive testing of new architecture
  5. Migration & Cleanup (2 weeks) - Remove legacy components and finalize

  Key Changes Identified

  The refactor transforms the current complex bash-orchestrated system into a cleaner Registry Module + Executive architecture:

  - Registry Module handles activation lifecycle decisions in Rust
  - New activation binary replaces parts of flox-activations
  - Executive (enhanced watchdog) manages process supervision
  - Simplified bash scripts use environment snapshots and replay
  - Consolidated activation flow removes complexity

  The plan includes comprehensive testing strategy, risk mitigation, and success criteria to ensure the refactor maintains all existing functionality while improving maintainability and performance.

